# MTA subway data reference

Use this when changing route/station mappings, GTFS parsing, or subway alerts.

## Runtime data files

- `lib/station-to-routes.json` – station metadata and route lists (northbound/southbound included)
- `lib/route-headsigns.json` – route terminal headsigns by direction
- `gtfs_subway/*.txt` – raw GTFS static source files

## Runtime modules

- `lib/subway-data.ts`
  - `getStation(stopId)`
  - `getRoutesForStation(stopId)`
  - `getNorthboundRoutesForStation(stopId)`
  - `getSouthboundRoutesForStation(stopId)`
  - `searchStationsByName(query)`
  - `getRouteColor(routeId)`
  - `getDirectionLabel(direction, arrivals)`
- `lib/subway-parser.ts`
  - parses GTFS-Realtime trip updates into arrivals
  - parses GTFS-Realtime alerts into normalized alert objects
- `app/api/subway-times/route.ts`
  - fetches required MTA feed groups based on station routes
  - fetches dedicated subway alerts feed
  - returns deduplicated active alerts + sorted arrivals

## Behavior notes

1. Real-time stop IDs include direction suffix (`N`/`S`), e.g. `F24N`; station IDs in mappings do not.
2. Alerts with empty `affectedRoutes` are treated as system-wide.
3. Alert dedupe is performed by both alert ID and normalized text content.
4. Feed selection is route-based (`ROUTE_TO_FEED` in the API route).

## Regenerate mappings

When GTFS files under `gtfs_subway/` are updated:

```bash
npx tsx lib/gtfs-mappings.ts
```

This regenerates:
- `lib/station-to-routes.json`
- `lib/route-headsigns.json`
